WEBVTT

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.200
It goes back and forth.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.250
The outcome of Akagi and Ichikawa's 
death match is completely unpredictable.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.260
But it seems as if the battle 
has entered the final throes.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.260
Ichikawa accepted Akagi's proposal,

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:29.260
and the match resumes with each 
player's points cut down to one tenth.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:35.270
Akagi has 6,800 and 
Ichikawa has 8,100 points.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.050
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.050
<b>An Innocent Devil</b>

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.170
What's going to happen?

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.910
There's no use discussing it now.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.350
They've both been reduced 
to under 10,000 points.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.020
We might have a winner after this hand.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.520
That's...

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.410
<i>But the flow is on Akagi's side.</i>

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.040
<i>He could just win this 
whole thing, here and now.</i>

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:03.530
Riichi.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.060
<i>Yes, the flow favors Akagi.</i>

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.100
<i>With a high end win, 
he could get a haneman.</i>

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.540
<i>Good fortune.</i>

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.060
<i>If he wins here, he wins it all.</i>

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.340
Ron!

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.680
But, of course, it was Ichikawa 
who put a stop to that.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.350
He dealt into the hand 
of the player after him.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:25.080
Adding 900 since it's the third 
bonus hand, he pays out 3,500.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.690
He now has 4,600 left.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.420
Ichikawa knows that sacrifices are 
necessary in order to stop Akagi.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.270
But Akagi also lost his 1,000 riichi wager,

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:39.050
and in the next hand, he's forced to deal into 
someone's hand to foil Ichikawa's tenpai.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.170
The 1 han hand costs him 1,300.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.900
He now has 4,500 points left.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.860
They are both under 5,000.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.120
Should either of them score a 5,200 hand,

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.180
the battle will be on a fast track 
to ending once and for all.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.360
Ichikawa draws on his years of experience.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.360
Akagi draws on his innate instinct.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.190
They read each other's hands 
and do not budge an inch.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.490
<i>The green dragon's a live tile.</i>

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.700
<i>Doesn't matter.</i>

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.160
Green dragon.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:09.900
Kan.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:13.900
Akagi.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.110
I don't want any arguing after I win,

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.870
so let me just make it clear right now.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.520
If I win right now from the 
tile I draw from the dead wall,

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.880
you alone must pay the full 
amount for dealing that live tile.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.800
I'm assuming you know that.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.080
Really?

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.690
Yeah, there's a rule for an open kan

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.890
where the person who dealt 
the tile has to pay for the win.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.690
But that almost never...

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.660
<i>Yes.</i>

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.100
<i>It almost never happens.</i>

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.930
<i>There is, though, 
the possibility, however slight.</i>

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.660
<i>I just wanted to make sure you knew.</i>

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.090
Whoops.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.370
Looks like I drew it.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.380
White dragon, rinshan kaihou.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.380
Rinshan kaihou - Winning off the extra 
tile drawn when you declare a kan.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.520
Impossible!

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.920
Can you flip the new dora indicator, Akagi?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.890
If I have even one dora, 
it will go up to 6,400.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.730
Since you only have 4,500, you'll be dead.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.500
The new dora is the 1 of circles.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.800
Ichikawa has none of the new dora.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.280
We survived.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:36.810
He managed to escape death, 
but now Akagi's only got 1,300.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.510
The no-tenpai penalty could kill him.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.550
If there are no more tiles to draw and your hand is not 
in tenpai, you must pay 1,000 to each player in tenpai.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.550
He really has nowhere left to run.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.620
Ichikawa, the new dora is the 1 of circles.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.480
Figures, from the demon spawn.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.560
He's got demonic luck.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.520
<i>However, that ends now.</i>

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.580
<i>Be it in this hand or the next, you will die.</i>

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.240
<i>Your antics are well and good, but you've 
picked the wrong man to play them with.</i>

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.570
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.070
<i>Akagi's figured it out.</i>

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.480
For a player of Ichikawa's caliber,

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.730
memorizing the tiles in his 
own wall is not a big feat.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:15.580
The 17 tiles in his wall, 
and the actual tile he drew.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.080
And that sleight of hand...

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.480
This lets him pick any of the 18 tiles he likes.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.100
Virtually invincible.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.830
Mind if I get some fresh air?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.450
Not at all.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.540
He cheated?

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.160
You may have done it 
to shorten the game,

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.540
but still, you started it.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.800
That was your fatal mistake.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.550
Ichikawa hadn't cheated because

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.600
he considered himself to be 
in a higher class than you.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.730
But what you did gave 
him an excuse to cheat.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:55.850
Can you beat him if he does stuff like that?!

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.560
Depends on the dice.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:04.100
If the wall stays intact in front of 
Ichikawa when the next hand starts,

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.570
he won't show mercy.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.130
He'll win on the fourth 
rotation with a tsumo.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.000
The fourth rotation?!

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:14.180
If that happens, 
the heavens have abandoned us.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:16.510
Let's just be prepared.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.990
But if the opposite of that happens,

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.090
and he's not able to pull any tricks,

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.060
I'll think of it as me 
having the advantage.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:31.020
If that happens,
 the heavens have chosen me.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.740
Telling me to win.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.030
The final moment draws closer.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:48.040
In order to survive, Akagi first 
entrusts his life to the dice.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.230
If that dice roll is in Ichikawa's favor,

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.780
Akagi's loss will have 
already been decided.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:57.520
Which means the death of 
Yasuoka and Nangou, as well.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.400
The rules call for two rolls of the dice.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.520
As the dealer, Ichikawa rolls 
the dice first and gets a 3, 4.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.340
The roll indicates the 
player opposite to him.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.830
The dice of fate are entrusted to Akagi.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:20.150
<i>Three!</i>

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:21.450
<i>Thank God.</i>

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.830
<i>Akagi's still got some luck.</i>

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.600
<i>And right when I think that, this?!</i>

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.880
<i>What a lousy starting hand.</i>

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:36.640
<i>He'll just have to do the best he can.</i>

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:42.120
<i>There's no guarantee that the wall 
won't be in front of Ichikawa next time.</i>

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:47.520
<i>How can he possibly turn this into a 
mangan hand to defeat Ichikawa?</i>

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:53.150
<i>How should he play to confuse 
Ichikawa into playing into his hand?</i>

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:55.690
Akagi's hand is no easy trial.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:56.540
And Ichikawa...

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:01.180
<i>Akagi's only got 1,300 left.</i>

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.600
<i>I didn't need these dora right now.</i>

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.550
<i>A lighter, faster hand 
would have been good.</i>

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.910
<i>There's no need to push myself here.</i>

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:13.560
<i>I can end this in one second if my 
wall is in front of me in the next hand.</i>

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.930
<i>What's important now 
is to not play into his hand.</i>

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:21.560
2 of circles.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.060
Chi.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:25.800
6 of characters.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:27.790
<i>A circles straight hand, huh?</i>

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:30.810
3 of characters!

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.310
Chi.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:34.810
1 of circles.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.980
<i>A called sanshoku?</i>

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.050
<i>Not a hand that leads to a mangan.</i>

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:45.050
<i>He just wants to win this hand, 
no matter how cheap the hand.</i>

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.710
<i>Three dora?</i>

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:55.980
<i>Which means the most he can have 
is a sanshoku with one dora.</i>

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.530
<i>Is he mocking me?!</i>

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.270
<i>If that's the case, 
I've got nothing to fear.</i>

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.510
Pon.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:10.780
<i>I won't hold back.</i>

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:11.760
<i>I will attack!</i>

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.850
Ichikawa is in tenpai.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:16.250
He has an ideal 2, 5, 8 of circles wait.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.970
<i>It's finally time to sign his death warrant.</i>

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:24.290
<i>He doesn't even have to deal into my hand.</i>

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:29.310
<i>He's only got 1,300 left. 
If I get so much as a tsumo, he's dead.</i>

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.920
<i>Why's he wavering now?</i>

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.020
<i>Even if he plays into it, 
it's only a sanshoku with one dora.</i>

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.510
<i>Only 2,000 points.</i>

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.040
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.510
<i>Normally, this north wind 
wouldn't be a threat.</i>

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.530
<i>However, if three coincidences 
were to come together,</i>

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:52.520
<i>it could possibly be a mangan hand.</i>

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:57.770
<i>If he discards the north wind and 
Akagi wins, there is nothing to fear.</i>

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.800
<i>The problem is that it would 
give Akagi an open kan.</i>

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:05.030
<i>The same trick Ichikawa used last hand 
to make Akagi pay for the win.</i>

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.450
<i>He'd have a rinshan kaihou, 
tsumo, and a sanshoku</i>

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.590
<i>worth two han, and any 
new dora on top of that.</i>

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.960
<i>Should that transform any pair in his hand,</i>

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.270
<i>or the north wind, into dora, his 
hand would be more than a mangan.</i>

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:17.780
<i>And this time, it would be 
Ichikawa's responsibility to pay.</i>

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:21.070
Of course, the chance of this 
happening is extremely low.

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:23.430
First, Akagi would have to 
declare a kan on the north wind.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.070
He would have to win with 
a tsumo from the dead wall,

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.170
as well as get new doras 
from the revealed tile.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.980
It would be a miracle that would require

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.030
passing through three separate barriers.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:34.340
Normally, discarding the north wind 
at this point would be no problem.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.920
But Ichikawa is afraid.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:38.850
That's right.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:41.620
The opponent Ichikawa faces is Akagi.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:46.500
He makes the improbable and 
the impossible possible.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:49.950
He is a man who can make 
you feel that fear.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.330
That's Akagi.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.510
From one moment to the next, 
Ichikawa is backed against the wall.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.680
What drives him into the corner 
is the live north wind tile.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:07.320
Should he keep it and discard 
a red dragon instead?

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:10.570
But that kind of playing 
style is too timid for him.

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:13.760
Even if they move into the next hand,
there is no telling which of them will win.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.910
<i>Anyone with common sense wouldn't 
even consider the possibility...</i>

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:23.330
<i>But this kid here can't be 
measured with common sense.</i>

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:27.000
<i>The next tile in my wall 
is the 3 of bamboo.</i>

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.010
<i>There is a possibility that 
it could be his winning tile.</i>

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:44.090
Kan!

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:46.990
<i>There it is!</i>

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:48.500
<i>I can't believe this kid!</i>

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.330
<i>Does he really intend to break through
those barriers and achieve the miracle?</i>

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.360
Right then, Ichikawa...

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.810
This is Ichikawa's plan.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.450
When he discarded the north wind,

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.240
he already had the red 
dragon hidden in his hand.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.150
If Akagi declared a kan,

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:08.870
he would replace the tile in the 
dead wall with this red dragon

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.750
and kill his chance at 
a rinshan kaihou win.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.370
Ichikawa's decision to discard the 
north wind was not just a bold play.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:18.490
It came with full insurance, 
covering all possibilities.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.230
<i>What's this hand?</i>

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.230
<i>That little...</i>

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.830
<i>He saw through my plan to 
switch the tile he'd draw...</i>

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.240
<i>Well, then...</i>

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.540
I've called three times now.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:38.280
And now for my dead wall draw.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.520
<i>That tile is the 3 of bamboo.</i>

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.520
<i>If he is ready, he could win with a sanshoku.</i>

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.520
<i>But the odds of that happening 
are less than one in three.</i>

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.760
<i>Like he will.</i>

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.440
What?!

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:05.730
In this moment, at the bottom 
of his heart, Ichikawa trembled

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.770
in fear of Akagi's luck.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:11.780
His actions before had 
already been a last resort.

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:13.530
If he couldn't switch Akagi's drawn tile,

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.680
he'd switch the new dora indicator tile.

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:19.920
Akagi can't get a mangan so long 
as he has less than two dora.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.630
There is a white dragon in Akagi's discards.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.260
Which means that if he switches 
the tile with a red dragon,

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.570
there's no way that Akagi 
will have any new dora.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.400
It is a perfect mangan blocker.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.860
However, the actual dora indicator tile

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:35.100
he switched out right then was the...

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.010
West wind!

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:43.070
Meaning, the four north winds 
would've given Akagi four dora.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:46.420
<i>I'd be dead if I hadn't made that switch.</i>

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.790
<i>This is scary.</i>

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.080
<i>This kid is unbelievable.</i>

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:53.190
<i>His luck exceeds all expectations.</i>

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.320
<i>He really is possessed by the gods.</i>

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:00.560
<i>Still, however narrow the 
margin, I am still the victor.</i>

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:04.750
<i>When I switched the red dragon, 
I switched his luck, too, and evaded him.</i>

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:08.910
<i>He won't get any new dora, 
and with an open rinshan kaihou</i>

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:11.300
<i>and called sanshoku, 
his hand stops at 2,600 points.</i>

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:14.390
<i>I used up one of my nine lives with this...</i>

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:16.330
The new dora.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.310
R-Right.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:21.500
A red dragon...

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.630
So the new dora is the white dragon.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:24.600
What?

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:25.810
That's funny.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:26.520
Huh?

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:28.830
The way the game's been going,

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.250
I could've sworn it was 
going to be a north wind.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:35.270
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.330
That kind of shameless 
guesswork won't help you!

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:41.100
But it's all the same.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:46.870
Huh?

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.610
It can't be...

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.830
Wh-White dragons?!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.080
He has two dora as his pair?!

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.140
Rinshan tsumo! 
Sanshoku, with two dora.

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:03.940
That's a mangan!

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:05.640
It's over!

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:08.090
We won! We really won!

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.750
White dragons?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.190
That can't be!

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:20.210
Something that ridiculous just isn't possible!

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.200
Why do you have white 
dragons as your pair?

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.850
Do you mean to tell me

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:27.210
you threw away a white dragon 
from a concealed triplet?

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.510
It's a game where every han counts,

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:33.060
and you threw a dragon away 
after you had gotten three?!

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:37.380
How could you do something that irrational?

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:42.590
Rationality is a rule in your world.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.320
Sorry, but that's not a 
restriction that applies to me.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:50.630
Throwing yourself into absurdity 
is what gambling is all about.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.710
You bastard!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:57.080
You laid that white dragon down as bait!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.470
You laid it down to force 
me to switch those tiles!

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:03.150
You did it on purpose!

00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:08.310
Akagi baited a trap.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:12.540
He did this to make Ichikawa 
believe he had no white dragons.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.470
He discarded a white dragon 
from a concealed triplet,

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:19.360
a move that is normally inconceivable.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:23.490
It was a decoy he employed based on his 
predictions of Ichikawa's future moves.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.330
On the one hand, 
Ichikawa had a hidden strategy

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.600
to prevent Akagi from 
getting his mangan hand

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.700
with multiple levels of insurance.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:37.160
Ichikawa was certain that 
he had evaded danger.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:41.050
However, a moment later, 
he'd be taught otherwise.

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:47.120
He had been dancing on Akagi's 
palm this entire time.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:52.560
<i>Akagi's win can't be written 
off as pure luck, after all.</i>

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.990
<i>His technique is superior.</i>

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.200
<i>His potential is superior.</i>

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.790
<i>He has natural genius.</i>

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:01.110
<i>A talent no one can even 
hope to come close to.</i>

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:04.480
<i>And it was too much for Ichikawa.</i>

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.810
Here's the eighty million, Akagi.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.280
Please take it.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:16.590
I don't want it.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:17.950
Double or nothing.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:21.530
Akagi!

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:23.220
Don't you know you when to quit?!

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:25.050
I never did.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:30.180
This game always was about playing 
until one of us is destroyed.

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.890
It was that kind of gamble.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.030
Right, Kurosaki-san?

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:38.610
Akagi...

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:42.810
I want to agree with you, but that's 
not how this is going to go.

00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:47.050
I didn't think Ichikawa would lose...

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.970
and we don't have another player.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.890
What are you talking about?

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:54.820
Why don't we just have a 
rematch with Ichikawa-san?

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.280
We were evenly matched.

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.060
He's done for.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.800
This game's made made it apparent 
that you belong in different leagues.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:10.080
He'll never be able to 
beat you in this lifetime.

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:14.060
That is to say, now that 
you've defeated Ichikawa,

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:16.400
we don't have any more 
chance of winning.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.170
I'm sorry to say it, but we're out.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:21.960
That's our final decision.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.010
This is good enough, right, Akagi?

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:26.860
Let's call it a day here.

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:31.500
I can set up other matches like this 
for you whenever you want.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.430
Okay?

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.670
Here you go, Nangou-san. Your cut.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.080
Akagi,

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.790
this is your cut.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.560
It's way too much for 
a middle school student.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.920
<i>The expression on Akagi's face 
then left an impression on me.</i>

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:10.090
<i>I still remember it to this day.</i>

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:13.570
<i>He had the eyes of a child who 
had lost interest in a toy.</i>

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.830
<i>The insanity housed in them had vanished.</i>

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:19.130
<i>His eyes were pure.</i>

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:21.490
<i>Yes, at a glance,</i>

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:25.070
<i>he was just another 13 year old 
middle school student.</i>

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:28.020
<i>It was like the demon had left him.</i>

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:33.950
<i>That's when I suddenly realized the 
secret behind Akagi's strength.</i>

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:38.510
<i>I realized what it is that he has, and I lack.</i>

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:43.720
<i>I decided that I wouldn't 
gamble ever again.</i>

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:47.000
<i>I could never be successful at gambling.</i>

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:53.560
<i>Because I'll never be able to have 
that sort of look in my eyes.</i>

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.600
The night of legend was over.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.610
<b>1963 (5 years later)</b>

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:07.900
Thanks.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:08.850
Thank you!

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.310
<i>It's been five years since then.</i>

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:22.830
<i>Yasuoka-san is still somewhat 
involved in gambling.</i>

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:26.170
<i>I got out of it.</i>

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:30.470
<i>I occasionally play Mahjong 
for fun, but not for money.</i>

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:33.580
<i>I haven't heard anything about Akagi.</i>

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:36.470
<i>He just disappeared.</i>

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:41.280
<i>Has he amassed an immense 
fortune by now?</i>

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:47.540
<i>Or did he get burned by 
the flame of gambling?</i>

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:50.490
Akagi...

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.490
And thus Akagi became a legend.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:59.670
But Akagi hadn't disappeared.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:03.500
The world would know about Akagi again.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.510
In just one short year.

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.200
Next time: "The Sign of Rebirth."

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Sign of Rebirth</b>
